  "notes": "Modified cash basis audit. Trim has 9 pages: Statement of Net Position (p1), Statement of Activities (p2-3), governmental funds assets/fund balances (p4) and receipts/expenditures (p5), proprietary Statement of Net Position (p6, accrual), proprietary revenues/expenses (p7, accrual), cash flows (p8), all-funds budgetary comparison (p9). Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5); transfers as the printed Total-column net 'Transfers From (To) Other Funds' (168,546) out, all to the Utilities Fund (fund columns: Street in 2,870, General out 34,412, Non-Major out 137,004, kept per fund in detail). Business-type from the Proprietary Fund Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p7, accrual-style: depreciation, capital assets, bonds), measure net position (1,636,190 -> 1,881,794), as in FY2024; the government-wide business-type column (p1-3) is cash-based (1,304,868 -> 1,520,224) and differs. Proprietary cash flow statement (p8) not recorded (proprietary field is GAAP-only, as FY2024). beginning_cash null (no prior-year cash printed); fund balances from p5; ending cash/investments are the sums of the printed governmental cash and investment lines (p4). Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds statement of assets and fund balances (p4), business-type lines from p1 business-type column. Detail is per fund column of the governmental funds statement (General, Street, Non-Major) and the Utilities Fund from the proprietary fund statement (p7, every printed row); the all-funds budgetary comparison schedule (p9, single combined column, unaudited) is not recorded in detail. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
